cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use pdfnative in academic work or cite it in publications,
  please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "pdfnative — Zero-dependency native PDF generation library"
abstract: >-
  A zero-dependency, pure-TypeScript library for generating ISO 32000-1 (PDF 1.7)
  compliant PDF documents with first-class support for Unicode text shaping
  across 27 scripts (Thai, Lao, Khmer, Myanmar, CJK, Arabic, Hebrew, Devanagari,
  Bengali, Tamil, Tai Tham, Cham and more, with a data-driven Universal Shaping
  Engine), typographic layout (paragraph breaking, justification, kerning,
  OpenType features), tagged PDF/UA, PDF/A-1b/2b/2u/3b, PDF/X-4 with CMYK colour,
  AES-128/256 encryption, AcroForm, digital signatures (RSA + ECDSA P-256) with
  PAdES long-term validation, barcodes, SVG rendering, and streaming output.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Nizoka"
    email: "hello@pdfnative.dev"
    website: "https://pdfnative.dev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nizoka/pdfnative"
url: "https://pdfnative.dev"
license: MIT
version: 1.8.0
date-released: 2026-09-14
keywords:
  - pdf
  - pdf-generation
  - typescript
  - iso-32000
  - unicode
  - text-shaping
